This data analytics project explores the global startup investment ecosystem to analyze funding patterns and predict company success using a Crunchbase dataset spanning from 1990 to 2014. The technical architecture features a complete data pipeline, starting with ETL processes developed in Databricks (PySpark) that feed into a PostgreSQL Star Schema Data Warehouse. The project incorporates machine learning models, utilizing a Gradient Boosting classifier to predict whether a startup will be acquired or closed (achieving an AUC of 0.78), and K-Means clustering to segment startups based on their funding profiles. The final insights are visualized through interactive Power BI dashboards, providing actionable intelligence on market trends, geographic concentration, and investment strategies.
